      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "A number is divisible by 3 if the sum of all the digits in the number is divisible by 3.\n\nA number is divisible by 6 if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.\n\nFirst, we need to find the greatest possible number that is divisible by 6. A number is divisible by 6 if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.\n\nA number is divisible by 2 if the ones digit is divisible by 2.\n\nA number is divisible by 3 if the sum of all the digits in the number is divisible by 3.\n\nLet us start from the hundreds digit and write the greatest possible number that is divisible by 3, 6, and 9:\n\nThe number is 609. 1+9 = 10, so add 2 to 10, and the ones place becomes 10+2 = 12. This is divisible by 3, 6, and 9.\n\nThis means the greatest possible three-digit number that is divisible by 3 and 6 is 609.",
